# Misc API keys for individual TOOLS -- NOT LLM provider keys.
#
# LLM provider credentials (OpenAI, Anthropic, etc.) live in providers.json,
# managed by credentials.py -- they are NOT read from here. This file is
# exclusively for one-off secrets that a specific tool needs to call some
# third-party grounding/research service.
#
# ONE KEY HERE IS READ TODAY: OPENALEX_API_KEY, by the scholarly lookup
# (ROADMAP_v3 §107), and only while `scholar_lookup: true` is set in
# config.yaml. It is optional -- the lookup runs keyless without it, on a
# far smaller daily budget -- and it is sent only to
# https://api.openalex.org, in a header, never in a URL. No shipped TOOL
# reads this file yet (#210), so GITHUB_API_TOKEN and NVD_API_KEY below are
# stored on disk for nothing; leave them out.
#
# Copy this file to .env and fill in only the keys you use. A variable of
# the same name in the environment wins over this file. Leave the rest
# blank -- env_secrets.get_env_secret() will raise a clear error at the
# point of use if a tool needs a key you never set, rather than failing
# silently with an empty string.

OPENALEX_API_KEY=
GITHUB_API_TOKEN=
NVD_API_KEY=
